<<~ ahu #/meme-header>>

! Meme — Extended Docs

This file does not bind invariant law.
Law lives in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme`.
This surface carries examples, tables, and split residue.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/required-shape-reference>>

!! Required Shape Reference

| surface | why it matters |
|---|---|
| doctype | marks the carrier as memetic-wikitext before active sigils appear |
| opener | declares the live address of the carrier |
| `#meta` | names identity, ratings, and role |
| title + opening scope | tells the reader what governs here and what does not |
| body thresholds | marks active semantic span |
| six-glyph phase map | binds the working loop compactly |
| edges | exposes adjacency explicitly |
| return throat | leaves residue honest |

Filled optional depth sharpens a meme.
It does not replace these surfaces.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/lifecycle-table>>

!! Lifecycle Table

| posture | reading |
|---|---|
| Noise | signal appears, but the copy-shape does not yet bind it |
| Data | machine-usable structure appears, but meme law still does not fully hold |
| Meme | minimum lawful shape now holds |
| Typed Meme | one or more outward type laws now bind the carrier |
| Canon Typed Meme | external ratification confirms the type bundle |

`confidence` reports the operator-facing band.
`mana`, `manao`, and `manaoio` keep their own jobs.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/resolution-notes>>

!! Resolution Notes

When a meme declares depth through named `pranala` sugar such as `loulou`, keep these states distinct:

| state | meaning | effect |
|---|---|---|
| resolved | target yields lawful content | raises trust in the outward claim |
| declared-unresolved | target named, but not yet yielding | creates explicit backlog pressure |
| absent | no outward claim declared | keeps the carrier shallow but honest |

Do not use outward depth callouts to restate a local anchor.
Do not treat decorative motion as structural depth.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/example-skeleton>>

!! Example Skeleton Reading

The copy-ready skeleton now lives in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme/SKILL` because it functions as working procedure, not invariant law.
Use that skeleton when you need a fresh lawful parent.
Then tighten its role, edges, and phase map for the actual carrier you are drafting.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/migration-note>>

!! Migration Note

This docs companion formed during the 2026-04-21 yin split/refine/clean pass.
The old parent mixed invariant law, phase-by-phase procedure, skeleton blocks, resolution detail, and research backlog.
The current shape keeps:

* parent invariant at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme`
* operational procedure at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme/SKILL`
* extended guidance here

Research backlog and subtype-specific detail should deepen into their own outward loci rather than re-swelling the parent.

<<~/ahu>>

